206AU cQ $|DQ(|b{+-})=300, |DS(n)=360, |DS(p)=420, |DQ(|a)=420 (syst,2021Wa16)  
206AU cQ $S(2n)=9940 {I360}, S(2p)=19200 {I500}, Q(|b{+-}n)=30 {I300}           
206AU2cQ (syst,2021Wa16)                                                        
206AU c  2015Mo20: {+9}Be target, 2.5 g/cm{+2} thick, was bombarded with a 1    
206AU2c  GeV/nucleon {+238}U pulsed beam at GSI in 3 and 4 s repetition         
206AU3c  cycles, and extraction times of 1 and 2 s, respectively. The {+206}Au  
206AU4c  recoiling nuclei were selected using the Fragment Separator (FRS)      
206AU5c  using three magnetic settings centered around {+205}Pt, {+215}Pb and   
206AU6c  {+217}Pb. The {+206}Au recoils were decelerated in an Al degrader      
206AU7c  before their implantation in an active stopper consisting of six DSSD  
206AU8c  detectors (256 pixels with 9 mm{+2} active area), surrounded by an     
206AU9c  array of 15 HPGe detectors (RISING). Measured: E|g, I|g and |b|g(t)    
206AUac  with a coincidence window of 100 |ms.                                  
206AU c  Other: 2017Ca12                                                        
206AU  L 0.0         (5+,6+)            40 S     15                             
206AU2 L %B-=100                                                                
206AU cL E$Early identification in 2009St16, 2008StZY, but no level properties  
206AU2cL were measured                                                          
206AU cL %B-$Neutron-rich nuclide with |b{+-} decay being the only expected     
206AU2cL decay mode                                                             
206AU cL J$Possible direct |b{+-}-decay feeding to the J|p=5- level in {+206}Hg 
206AU2cL (2015Mo20). Particle-hole character of the proposed configuration      
206AU3cL (repulsive for mutual alignment) would be consistent with J|p=5+,6+.   
206AU3cL The authors of 2015Mo20 proposed a tentative J|p=(4+,5+) assignment.   
206AU cL T$From sum of |b{+-}-gated 1068|g(t) and 1034|g(t) spectra in 2015Mo20 
206AU2cL and the maximum likelihood method. The uncertainty includes both       
206AU3cL statistical and systematics components, but the individual             
206AU4cL contributions were not given by the authors. Other: 56 s {I17} from    
206AU5cL |b{+-}(t) in 2017Ca12.                                                 
206AU cL CONF$|p(d{-3/2}){+-1}~#|n(g{-9/2}){++1}. The |p(d{-3/2}){+-1} orbital  
206AU2cL is associated with the ground state of the even-N Au nuclei, while the 
206AU3cL |n(g{-9/2}){++1} orbital is associated with the ground state of the    
206AU4cL {+209}Pb and {+211}Po (N=127) isotopes. If J|p=5+, admixtures with the 
206AU5cL |p(s{-1/2}){+-1}~#|n(g{-9/2}){++1} configuration are possible.         
206AU6cL The authors of 2015Mo20 proposed a tentative                           
206AU7cL configuration=|p(s{-1/2}){+-1}~#|n(g{-9/2}){++1}                       

