206PO c  2016Gr17: 2.85 MeV/nucleon {+206}Po beam produced in UC{-x}(p,X),E=1.4 
206PO2c  GeV at ISOLDE-CERN facility. The polonium atoms were ionized using the 
206PO3c  resonant-ionization laser ion source (RILIS), mass selected using the  
206PO4c  ISOLDE High Resolution Separator (HRS), and finally injected in the    
206PO5c  REX-ISOLDE accelerator complex. Targets comprised of 2 mg/cm{+2}-thick 
206PO7c  {+104}Pd and {+114}Cd foils. Measured E|g, I|g, scattered projectile   
