206RN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=F.G. KONDEV$CIT=NDS 201, 346 (2025)$CUT=21-Jan-2025$       
206RN c  1981Ri02: {+206}Fr produced by Ir({+20}Ne,xn) reaction on natural      
206RN2c  target with E({+20}Ne)|?115 MeV followed by isotope separation. Ge(Li) 
206RN3c  and Si(Li) detectors were used to measure |g and ce spectra, and       
206RN4c  |g|g coincidences.                                                     
206RN c  The decay scheme involves decay of two states in {+206}Fr with J|p=3+  
206RN2c  and 7+. This is confirmed by the |b{++}+|e feedings to low spin        
206RN3c  2+ and 4+ levels, as well as to high-spin 6+ and 8+ states.            
206RN4c  The large Q value in the |b{++}+|e decay of {+206}Fr suggests that     
206RN5c  many other, yet unobserved, states are populated. The |b{++}+|e        
206RN6c  feedings and corresponding log| {Ift} values could not be determined   
206RNxc  unambiguously                                                          
