206RN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=F.G. KONDEV$CIT=NDS 201, 346 (2025)$CUT=21-Jan-2025$       
206RN c  2003He06: Source produced using {+204}Pb({+12}C,6n) reaction.          
206RN2c  Projectile: E({+12}C)=78-110 MeV, beam intensity 100-200 pnA. Target:  
206RN3c  enriched to 99.73% {+204}Pb, 0.45 mg/cm{+2} thick, evaporated on carbon
206RN4c  layers of 0.04 mg/cm{+2} (upstream) and covered with 0.005 mg/cm{+2}   
206RN5c  carbon (downstream), mounted on a rotating wheel (50 Hz repetition     
206RN6c  frequency) and synchronized with the beam time macro structure.        
206RN7c  Detectors: velocity filter SHIP, position sensitive 16-strip detector  
206RN8c  (PIPS) with a typical resolution of 20-24 keV. HPGe detector located   
206RN9c  behind PIPS. Measured: E|a, I|a; E|a-E|g correlations.                 
206RN c  1967Va22: Source produced using {+197}Au({+19}F,6n) and                
206RN2c  {+206}Pb({+12}C,8n) reactions. Projectiles: E({+19}F)=197 MeV and      
206RN3c  E({+12}C)=125 MeV. Targets: {+197}Au, 2.5 mg/cm{+2} thick and enriched 
206RN4c  to 97.22% {+206}Pb, 0.3 mg/cm{+2} thick. Detectors: Si (Au) surface    
206RN5c  barrier detectors. Measured: E|a, I|a, T{-1/2}.                        
