206RN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=F.G. KONDEV$CIT=NDS 201, 346 (2025)$CUT=21-Jan-2025$       
206RN c  1981Ho29: {+197}Au({+14}N,5n|g) reaction with E({+14}N)=80-94 MeV and  
206RN2c  {+194}Pt({+16}O,4n|g) reaction on enriched (97%) target with           
206RN3c  E({+16}O)=85-110 MeV. The targets were backed with 8-10 mg/cm{+2}      
206RN4c  thick {+208}Pb layers; Detectors: Ge(Li); Measured: excitation         
206RN5c  functions, E|g, I|g, |g|g(t) coin, T{-1/2}; Deduced: level scheme. No  
206RN6c  longer-lived isomers (T{-1/2}<0.05 s) were observed in a pulsed beam   
206RNxc  experiment                                                             
206RN c  1981Ma28: {+198}Hg({+12}C,4n|g), E({+12}C)=80 MeV with 85.3% enriched  
206RN2c  {+198}Hg target cooled at -30|' C. The beam was pulsed with 1 ns width 
206RN3c  separated by 1.5 |ms periods. Detectors: two Ge(Li); Measured:         
206RN4c  E|g, I|g, |g(t) I(t,|q), angular distributions, g-factors, T{-1/2};    
206RN5c  Deduced: |m                                                            
206RN c  2008An01,2008Kr01: {+197}Au({+14}N,5n|g), E({+14}N)=82 MeV.            
206RN2c  Target: 3 mg/cm{+2}; OSIRIS-II gamma-ray spectrometer consisting of 10 
206RN3c  HPGe detectors and internal electron conversion spectrometer with two  
