206AC c  2014Zh03: {+206}Ac produced by bombarding a 400 |mg/cm{+2} thick       
206AC2c  {+169}Tm target covered with a 10 |mg/cm{+2} carbon layer with         
206AC3c  196 MeV {+40}Ca beam at HIRFL in Lanzhou. Evaporation residues were    
206AC4c  separated in flight using the SHANS recoil separator, and implanted    
206AC5c  into position sensitive silicon detectors. The |a particles            
206AC6c  were detected by eight non-position sensitive Si detectors with        
206AC7c  FWHM=70 keV for 6-7 MeV |a's. Three |a-decay chains were observed with 
206AC8c  E|a(1)[{+206}Ac]=7817 keV {I30}, E|a(2)[{+202}Fr]=7245 keV {I30} and   
206AC9c  E|a(3)[{+198}At]=6775 keV {I30} with half-lives of 41 ms {I+56-15},    
206ACAc  0.29 s {I+40-11} and 3.1 s {I+56-12}, respectively.                    
206AC c  1998Es02: Activity produced by bombarding a 320 |mg/cm{+2} thick       
206AC2c  {+175}Lu target with 199 MeV {+36}Ar ions. The reaction products were  
206AC3c  separated by the gas-filled separator (RITU) and implanted into a      
206AC4c  position sensitive PIPS detector (800 mm wide and 35 mm high).         
206AC5c  Separate amplified branches for energy ranges 0.5-15 MeV (|a-decay)    
206AC6c  and 2-200 MeV (reaction residues) were used. Two |a-decaying           
206AC7c  states were identified, one using 9 quadruple                          
206AC8c  (recoil-|a{-1}-|a{-2}-|a{-3}) and 2 triple (recoil-|a{-1}-|a{-3})      
206AC8c  (E|a{-2} missing) events: 7790 keV {I30} (|a{-1}), 7236 keV {I7}       
206AC9c  (|a{-2}), 6752 keV {I6} (|a{-3}) associated with the 3+ ground state   
206ACac  and the other using 5 quadruple and 1 triple (E|a{-2} missing) events: 
206ACbc  7750 keV {I20} (|a{-1}), 7248 keV {I13} (|a{-2}) and 6858 keV {I7}     
206ACcc  (|a{-3}) associated with the 10- isomer. The assignment to a           
206ACdc  specific state is based on the time and position correlations with     
206ACxc  known |a-decays of {+202}Fr, {+198}At and {+194}Bi                     
206AC c  1998LuZV: Activity produced by bombarding a 307 |mg/cm{+2} hafnium     
206AC2c  target (64.6% {+176}Hf,21.7% {+177}Hf, 6.8% {+178}Hf, 2.2% {+179}Hf    
206AC3c  and 4.7% {+180}Hf) with 186-MeV (effective energy at half-target       
206AC4c  thickness) {+35}Cl ions (beam intensity was about 600 enA). The        
206AC5c  reaction products were separated by a recoil mass separator at JAERI   
206AC6c  and implanted on a position-sensitive silicon detector. Two |a decaying
206AC7c  states were identified, one using 4 quadruple                          
206AC8c  (recoil-|a{-1}-|a{-2}-|a{-3}) and one triple (recoil-|a{-1}-|a{-2})    
